   "status": "UNCLEAR",
   "ruling": "Ruling: ambiguity; i4562 p. 4, Line 1: \"Generally, the maximum section 179 expense deduction is $2,500,000 for section 179 property (including qualified section 179 real property) placed in service during the tax year beginning in 2025.\"; \"Tip: You can use Worksheet 1 to assist you in determining the amount to enter on line 1.\"; Worksheet 1: \"3. Enter the smaller of line 1 or line 2 here ... 4. Enter the amount from line 3 here and on Form 4562, line 1\". The model reads Worksheet 1 as fixing line 1 at the smaller of the cost and $2,500,000; the project follows the line 1 instruction on the same page, which states the maximum as $2,500,000 and offers the worksheet as an aid. amb.2025.s179_carryover_no_property records the model's reading as the alternative and the owner adopted the project's (TASKS T-043; ambiguities/research/amb.2025.s179_carryover_no_property.md). The English says what the project computes and names the register entry (\"Interpretation: amb.2025.s179_carryover_no_property\"); lines 5, 11 and 13 change with line 1 as the model says, by design.",
